          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "T_{1} = 1, T_{2} = 2, T_{3} = 4,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}-1}+\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}-2}+\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{n}-3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n \\geq 4 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{T}_{4}, \\mathrm{T}_{5}, \\mathrm{T}_{6}, \\mathrm{T}_{7}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { T } _ { \\mathrm { g } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.18,
            0.525,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.4 Arithmetic Progressions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.213,
            0.886,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So far we have learnt that a sequence is an ordered list of numbers that may follow a particular rule. However, there may be sequences, such as the sequence of prime numbers, where there is no clear regularity in the rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.292,
            0.885,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this section, we explore a special kind of sequence called an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "arithmetic progression",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.331,
            0.884,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first four stages of the pattern are shown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.38,
            0.856,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.141,
                0.38,
                0.856,
                0.589
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.338,
                0.601,
                0.66,
                0.619
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 8.3: Growing pattern of squares"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.633,
            0.884,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we count the number of tiny squares at each stage, we get sequence 1, 5, 9, 13."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.696,
            0.399,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.732,
            0.855,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you predict the number of squares in Stages 5 and 6 of the sequence? In Stages 10, 11 and 12? In Stage 20? At any stage?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.791,
            0.885,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We observe that at each stage, 4 squares get added to the corners of the pattern in the earlier stage. The number of squares at successive stages can be written as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.343,
            0.852,
            0.691,
            0.872
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "1,1+4,1+4+4,1+4+4+4,\\ldots"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
